   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Apposition",
     "texto": [
      "An apposition gives extra information about a noun and is set off by commas: **Mein Chef, Herr Müller, ist sehr nett** (my boss, Mr Müller, is very nice). The apposition has the same case as the noun it explains.",
      "If the apposition has an article and the name is repeated in another case, the case of the main noun is kept: **Ich helfe meinem Chef, Herrn Müller** (I help my boss, Mr Müller)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Beware of the false friend",
     "texto": [
      "In German, an apposition in the plural or with a proper name is placed between commas, just as in English. Do not confuse it with the relative clause: **Mein Chef, der nett ist** (my boss, who is nice) is relative. The apposition has no verb."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
